~ AgathaDayThree
set Player.canMove = false
set NPC.tempElapTime = NPC.elapsedTime
set NPC.tempCycProg = NPC.cycleProgress

Agatha seemed almost frantic, approaching me and speaking before I could even comprehend was was going on.
Agatha: "Mort... Something's up. I haven't seen Judith all day and when I knocked, she didn't answer. Ryan still isn't back from the city, either."
Mort: "Agatha, slow down, take a deep breath. Tell me what's going on slowly, okay?"
Agatha did a breathing exercise... and then another... and then three more before finally pulling out her inhaler and solving the actual problem.
Agatha: "I just... I usually know where everyone is and how everyone's doing and last time I didn't know where someone was, Harry-"
She stopped dead in her tracks, the both of us silent as a mouse. She didn't need to tell me what happened last time. Everyone here was at fault, but her most of all.
There was a reason I didn't trust in her ability to keep everyone safe.
There was a reason she was the last to go.
Mort: "I know you're worried, Agatha, but worrying like that isn't going to get us anywhere. No sense in going crazy. Ryan can handle himself and Judith can't get that far, I'm sure she's just sleeping in today, yeah?"
That seemed to calm Agatha down enough, but not completely. In fact, my calmness seemed to unease her.
I messed up, I reacted too calmly when she mentioned Harry. I thought tempering my reaction would assuade her anxiety but I only made her more suspicious.
Mort: "You're not the only one looking, okay? If we don't see them again by tomorrow, we'll go to the city and get some help, you and I, okay?"
Agatha looked at me with that same patient gaze, as if she was analyzing me. She had her moments of weakness, but damn she recovered quick.
Too quick for her own good.
Agatha: "Alright, Mortimer. I'll give it one more day. But just one. I know I get antsy but I always have cause."
Taking that as a sign to get out of here before I revealed my actions to any greater extent, I simply nodded as I took my leave. Just like I usually did with Agatha.

set NPC.elapsedTime = NPC.tempElapTime
set NPC.cycleProgress = NPC.tempCycProg
set NPC.isIdle = false
set NPC.canMove = true
set Player.canMove = true

=> END

